      "title": "Imran Khan’s party decries ‘coup’ after Pakistan suspends provincial government",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/12/imran-khans-party-decries-coup-after-pakistan-suspends-provincial-government",
      "description": "<p>Suspension of provincial government escalates standoff with Khan’s PTI party a week after his supporters began marching to demand his release</p><p>Pakistan has declared a state of emergency in a province ⁠led by Imran ​Khan’s PTI party and suspended its government, a move a party spokesperson described as “more of a coup disguised as emergency”.</p><p>President Asif Ali Zardari ​declared the emergency in the north-western Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province on Sunday, after the federal government said authorities there had failed to tackle Islamist militancy in the province bordering Afghanistan.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/12/imran-khans-party-decries-coup-after-pakistan-suspends-provincial-government\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
